error[E0248]: this `match` takes a `String` apart both with `[]` or `::` and with its constructors
 --> seq_patterns_errors.ck:9:9
  |
9 |         String b -> 0
  |         ^^^^^^^^ a constructor of `String`
  = note: `[]` and `x :: rest` take a `String` apart with `Seq.uncons`, not with its constructors
  = help: use one kind of pattern in each `match`

error[E0240]: this `match` does not cover `[]` or `_ :: _ :: _`
  --> seq_patterns_errors.ck:13:5
   |
13 |     match xs
   |     ^^^^^^^^ not exhaustive
   = help: add arms for these, or a catch-all `_ -> …`

error[E0240]: this `match` does not cover `_ :: []`
  --> seq_patterns_errors.ck:17:5
   |
17 |     match xs
   |     ^^^^^^^^ not exhaustive
   = note: counterexample: xs = b"\xad"
   = help: add an arm `_ :: [] -> …`, or a catch-all `_ -> …`

error[E0241]: `Nil` is a constructor of `List`, but the value being matched has type `Box`
  --> seq_patterns_errors.ck:26:9
   |
26 |         []     -> 0
   |         ^^ expected a `Box` pattern
   = help: `[]` and `x :: rest` take apart a list, or a value of a type with a `Seq` instance; `Box` has none

error[E0241]: `Cons` is a constructor of `List`, but the value being matched has type `Box`
  --> seq_patterns_errors.ck:27:9
   |
27 |         _ :: _ -> 1
   |         ^^^^^^ expected a `Box` pattern
   = help: `[]` and `x :: rest` take apart a list, or a value of a type with a `Seq` instance; `Box` has none

